/comments/3616042231","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113583#issuecomment-3616042231","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113583","id":3616042231,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XiGz3","user":{"login":"meitwouldseem","id":32341472,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzQxNDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32341472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem","html_url":"https://github.com/meitwouldseem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T09:39:41Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T09:39:41Z","body":"@AThousandShips I don't have an authoritative source on this, but to the best of my knowledge this is not how Vulkan is supposed to behave. It aught to be possible to send push constants without any padding. This would suggest that it's an engine bug rather than a documentation issue no? Sorry if I'm misinterpreting.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3616042231/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3616089673","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113583#issuecomment-3616089673","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113583","id":3616089673,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XiSZJ","user":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T09:53:07Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T09:53:07Z","body":"I don't know where the limitation comes from if it's engine or driver specific, we'll see what the rendering team says","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3616089673/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3616282525","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113583#issuecomment-3616282525","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113583","id":3616282525,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XjBed","user":{"login":"mrjustaguy","id":50302479,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUwMzAyNDc5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/50302479?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy","html_url":"https://github.com/mrjustaguy","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mrjustaguy/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T10:35:57Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T10:35:57Z","body":"It may be a limitation of APIs like DX12 and Metal as well, as it is the RD that's pushing the error, which is a wrapper for DX12, Vulkan and Metal (basically every modern low level API) so one or all of the APIs have issues with that","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3616282525/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3616639194","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113583#issuecomment-3616639194","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113583","id":3616639194,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7XkYja","user":{"login":"meitwouldseem","id":32341472,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyMzQxNDcy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32341472?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem","html_url":"https://github.com/meitwouldseem","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meitwouldseem/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T12:11:53Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T12:11:53Z","body":"IMO this will require either a way to query the expected push constant size from GDScript or for Godot to automatically add the padding internally.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3616639194/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3618547689","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/113583#issuecomment-3618547689","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/113583","id":3618547689,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7Xrqfp","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-12-05T20:43:29Z","updated_at":"2025-12-05T20:43:29Z","body":"Push constants follow the Vulkan memory layout rules described here: https://docs.vulkan.org/spec/latest/chapters/interfaces.html#interfaces-alignment-requirements\n\nThis memory layout matches the std430 layout used by OpenGL which is described nicely here: https://wikis.khronos.org/opengl/Interface_Block_(GLSL)#Memory_layout\n\nThe takeaway is that structs that are less than 16 bytes will be padded up to 16 bytes. This is very important if you have multiple structs in the same chunk of memory, but is less important for push constants since the memory for push constants is managed by the GPU driver. You just push the number of bytes that you care about. \n\nThat being said, Godot aims to be robust and cover multiple graphics APIs. It also needs to work on devices where the graphics drivers are buggy. Therefore, when it comes to things like memory layout, we choose to be explicit and correct instead of relying on GPU drivers to be perfect. The effect of being strict on memory layout is that anyone creating structs for push constants needs to be aware of and respect alignment and padding requirements. Which is something we want for our codebase. \n\nThat's all a question for our internal rendering backend though. It would have been a perfectly acceptable choice for us to add padding to push constants created through GDScript in this case. Trailing padding doesn't carry the same risks that internal padding does. \n\nIn my opinion, its an acceptable choice either way. Adding padding automatically is maybe slightly nicer for users who will only ever be passing a float or two to their shader. But it hides implementation details that are extremely important if you are passing anything more complex than a couple of floats. You can't hide padding rules from GDScript users since the definition of the push constant in the shader itself needs to take padding into consideration. \n\nOn the other hand, being strict about padding/alignment everywhere makes it super easy for us to validate that the data structure on the CPU matches the one on the GPU. We just check total size and then can easily provide the user with an error when the sizes don't match. Since the RD API is intended for advanced users who are willing to get their hands dirty, it makes sense to give them a low-level API and not try to hide any details by making things work automagically. \n\nThe docs could definitely have more info on alignment requirements, at the very least they could point to an external link that explains padding rules for users who are newer to GPU programming. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3618547689/reactions","total_count":3,"+1":2,"-1":1,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]